\section{Not yet verified}{
The spec records these as open. They are listed rather than hidden:

\itemize{
\item mzLib checks that the project exists only when the list's body is empty. A body that is only the header returns 0 rows without that check, so a header-only answer for an unknown accession would read as a project with no checksums. PRIDE has not been seen to send one: it answers an unknown accession with an empty body (PXD999999999, 2026-10-21).
\item No public project with an empty list has been found, so the 0-row answer is pinned by a stubbed test only, not by a recorded fixture.
}
}
